mode: "100644"
text: "# Pinterest 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly.*\n\n## The mindset: a visual search engine, not social media\nPinterest works like **Google for visuals.** Users arrive **with intent** (planning purchases,\nprojects, recipes, decor) — high purchase intent. Discovery is driven by **keywords, relevance, and\nvisual similarity — not who you follow.** So **followers matter far less than keyword structure and\nfresh pin designs**; small/new accounts can win on strong SEO + creative. (631M MAU, Q1 2026.)\n\n## Evergreen + compounding (the superpower)\nPins last **months to years** (vs 24–48h on IG/TikTok). A well-optimized pin keeps surfacing in search\nweeks/months later; old pins **regain relevance** when demand returns. You're building a **long-term\nsearchable traffic asset base.** Honest: traction usually takes **3–6 months**, then compounds.\n\n## Fresh pins are the #1 rule\nPinterest **heavily favors fresh content** — a new pin gets an early visibility boost and a few-day\n**test window** that determines long-term reach. \"Fresh\" = a **new image/layout/text overlay**, not a\nrepin. Make **3–5 visually distinct designs per destination** (each counts as fresh; the top 1% of\npins drive ~50% of traffic, so distinct designs raise your odds). **Fresh pin designs drive ~90% of\nwebsite traffic; saves/repins now have minimal ranking impact (2026).**\n\n## Keywords / SEO = the top ranking factor\nPinterest scans **pin title, description, board name, alt text, image file name, and linked domain.**\nFavor **long-tail, high-intent** phrases; 2026 uses **semantic matching** (entities/clusters), so\n**clarity beats cleverness** — make it unmistakably about a real search query. Research with **Pinterest\nTrends/Predicts, autocomplete, related pins** (ties to `social-seo`). **Hashtags are nearly dead\n(~1% of ranking power)** — deprioritize; 2–5 max if any.\n\n## Boards = topic clusters\nName boards with **specific, keyword-driven themes** (\"Eco-Friendly Gift Ideas for Men\", not\n\"Miscellaneous\"). Boards are **cluster/entity signals**; pick **one content pillar at a time**, build\nthemed boards under it, and pin **3–7 fresh pins/week per cluster.** Wrong cluster authority takes\nmonths to correct — structure it right from the start.\n\n## Specs + formats\n- **2:3 ratio (1000×1500) is essential** — other ratios are **penalized** (official guidance). Add a\n  **keyword text overlay.**\n- **Static pins** → most **traffic** (link out). **Video pins** (9:16, **6–15s**) → ~**2× engagement.**\n  **Idea Pins are retired** — Pinterest merged everything into one unified Pin format (old Idea Pins\n  became video pins), so **every pin can carry an outbound link now.** Collage/Rich/Product pins for\n  shopping.\n\n## Links — the differentiator\nUnlike X/IG, **Pinterest rewards outbound links** (\"free clicks\"). Link to a **relevant** product/blog/\nlanding page that delivers on the pin — **not your homepage** (users expect value after the click).\n\n## Cadence + seasonal\n**Steady, not bursts:** ~**3–10 fresh pins/day** (new accounts 3–5; established 5–10). **Don't** mass-pin\nthe same URL/board at once — **space ~72h between pins to the same URL** (spam filter). **Seasonal:\nlaunch 45–90 days before peak** (45% of users plan 60+ days ahead). Evergreen builds the library;\nseasonal captures the wave.\n\n## Fit + AI\nStrongest for **fashion, home/decor, DIY, food, beauty, weddings, lifestyle, e-commerce, gift guides,\nblog traffic.** Pinterest uses **GenAI** (custom product backgrounds, recommendations) and lets users\n**filter GenAI content** — disclose AI imagery. **FTC disclosure** required on affiliate pins.\n"
